WEBVTT

00:03.300 --> 00:05.520
<i>My name is Valefor.</i>

00:06.120 --> 00:10.530
<i>It's been one week since I was taken 
into confinement by an Archdemon.</i>

00:13.200 --> 00:14.950
<b>Valefor's Archdemon Observation Log</b>

00:15.590 --> 00:18.320
<i>With my roommate, Nephy,</i>

00:18.320 --> 00:22.670
<i>I've been doing work like cleaning,
 laundry, and preparing food.</i>

00:23.280 --> 00:25.420
<i>It's tiring, but no real pain.</i>

00:25.900 --> 00:28.820
<i>Mostly because if I do 
good work, I get praised.</i>

00:31.970 --> 00:36.360
<i>I have to say, I don't understand the
 Archdemon and Nephy's relationship.</i>

00:36.930 --> 00:40.100
<i>Every morning, Nephy goes to him.</i>

00:40.720 --> 00:46.100
<i>After staring at the Archdemon's face in the 
throne room, she begins her work for the day.</i>

00:46.700 --> 00:48.980
<i>I once decided to get closer 
to see what she was doing,</i>

00:49.450 --> 00:52.490
<i>but it looked like she was just 
watching him from different angles.</i>

00:53.150 --> 00:58.920
<i>As she did, Nephy's pointy 
ears started to wiggle.</i>

00:59.660 --> 01:02.080
<i>Then, she said in a quiet voice...</i>

01:02.080 --> 01:03.580
Tomorrow will be the day.

01:03.850 --> 01:06.770
<i>I thought that was interesting 
so I've made a note of it.</i>

01:08.070 --> 01:10.000
<i>Even if I don't understand why.</i>

01:11.500 --> 01:15.790
<i>The Archdemon spends all day inside his 
library reading through sorcery books.</i>

01:16.790 --> 01:22.720
<i>He also gives Nephy, who's his apprentice, 
hands-on lessons in sorcery.</i>

01:24.310 --> 01:29.310
<i>Another thing I don't understand 
is why she sits on his lap.</i>

01:29.620 --> 01:33.600
<i>He also keeps reaching out to Nephy's 
silver hair before pulling his hand away</i>

01:33.600 --> 01:35.790
<i>in this weird motion, over and over.</i>

01:36.350 --> 01:39.910
<i>Nephy looks anxious about it but not upset.</i>

01:44.980 --> 01:49.840
<i>I wondered if I had seen something 
I shouldn't have and braced myself for death.</i>

01:49.840 --> 01:50.880
<i>But...</i>

01:51.680 --> 01:54.510
<i>It doesn't look like
 I'm going to be punished.</i>

01:55.110 --> 01:57.840
<i>I wonder what I saw, then?</i>

01:57.840 --> 02:00.090
<i>I still don't have any answers.</i>

02:00.720 --> 02:06.310
<i>Still, living here gives me 
a warm feeling in my chest.</i>

02:07.090 --> 02:10.980
<i>And tomorrow, they're taking me 
to the old Archdemon's castle.</i>

03:41.030 --> 03:46.030
<b>Episode 8:
 I Found a Dragon and
I Guess She's My Daughter Now</b>

03:49.840 --> 03:52.460
So cute!

03:52.970 --> 03:55.040
I've even impressed with myself!

03:55.040 --> 03:56.920
Can I take her home with me?!

03:56.920 --> 04:00.010
Wait, other way around! 
Can you leave her here with me?!

04:00.010 --> 04:01.360
Simmer down!

04:01.360 --> 04:03.340
And she's not an object! 
I'm not handing her off!

04:06.290 --> 04:09.760
Thanks for shopping with us! Come again!

04:09.760 --> 04:12.630
Going to her store is always exhausting.

04:10.360 --> 04:11.870
I'll be waiting!

04:12.630 --> 04:16.730
But I think we made the right choice 
going to Miss Manuela's store.

04:17.080 --> 04:20.950
Well, she can't wander around in that armor.

04:20.950 --> 04:23.170
And considering she only had 
undergarments beneath her robe...

04:23.170 --> 04:24.240
Not that.

04:25.010 --> 04:25.770
Look.

04:34.110 --> 04:36.400
I think she likes her new outfit.

04:36.400 --> 04:37.300
Zagan.

04:38.790 --> 04:39.920
Thank you.

04:41.300 --> 04:44.170
W-Well, I'm glad you like it.

04:50.340 --> 04:52.720
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

04:52.720 --> 04:58.230
<i>It's different from how I care 
for Nephy, but oddly warm...</i>

04:59.120 --> 05:02.760
<i>Wait... is this a protective instinct?!</i>

05:03.210 --> 05:06.980
<i>Ridiculous. The idea of me developing 
that kind of sentiment...</i>

05:08.460 --> 05:12.840
<i>If Barbatos heard about this, 
he'd be worried about my head.</i>

05:20.780 --> 05:22.630
<i>I'm such a fool.</i>

05:23.160 --> 05:26.890
<i>I had to return my Sacred Sword. 
I can't wear anointed armor.</i>

05:27.420 --> 05:28.050
<i>But...</i>

05:28.750 --> 05:33.580
<i>My withdrawal will cause a major delay
 in the manhunt for the new Archdemon.</i>

05:33.580 --> 05:37.390
<i>Although I doubt he'd ever 
be grateful to me for it.</i>

05:38.000 --> 05:42.320
<i>Why did I feel compelled to do it, though?</i>

05:42.880 --> 05:46.000
<i>I don't intend on getting 
between the two of them.</i>

05:46.000 --> 05:49.100
<i>But I do want to see them living peacefully,</i>

05:49.100 --> 05:53.450
<i>and one day start a family, 
enjoying their lives together.</i>

05:56.730 --> 06:00.460
<i>And then... even if it's just occasionally,</i>

06:00.880 --> 06:03.850
<i>I'd be honored if they'd 
remember me once in a while.</i>

06:06.520 --> 06:10.500
I bet Zagan would be a doting father.

06:11.280 --> 06:13.600
Enjoying the new outfit?

06:11.280 --> 06:14.220
He's a kind man, deep down.

06:13.600 --> 06:14.220
Yeah.

06:14.560 --> 06:17.240
Yeah, just like that...

06:17.640 --> 06:19.270
Wait, Z-Zagan?!

06:20.150 --> 06:21.030
You...

06:22.820 --> 06:26.030
You two already went as 
far as to have a child?!

06:27.650 --> 06:32.140
D-D-Don't be so shameless! Nephy and 
I haven't done anything like that yet!

06:32.140 --> 06:33.990
Wait, "yet"?

06:34.650 --> 06:36.520
Zagan, who is this?

06:36.520 --> 06:39.290
Oh, sorry. That's a good point.

06:42.140 --> 06:43.420
Who are you?

06:44.430 --> 06:45.630
That's...

06:46.660 --> 06:49.330
You don't even remember me...

06:49.330 --> 06:52.470
Lord Zagan, Lord Zagan! It's Miss Chastille!

06:53.040 --> 06:58.140
Oh, right, you! You were dressed differently 
than usual, so I didn't realize.

06:58.480 --> 07:00.870
This is a friend of Nephy's.

07:00.870 --> 07:02.730
Why are you dressed like that?

07:02.730 --> 07:04.210
W-Well...

07:04.210 --> 07:05.960
Lady Chastille!

07:06.610 --> 07:08.480
It's dangerous to run around 
on your own like this!

07:08.480 --> 07:10.490
Wait, it's Zagan!

07:10.830 --> 07:13.240
Oh, it's the Three Cerulean Nerds.

07:13.240 --> 07:15.590
Three Cerulean Knights!

07:15.590 --> 07:18.500
What were you doing to Lady Chastille?!

07:18.940 --> 07:20.940
Not a thing, really—

07:24.180 --> 07:25.100
Don't.

07:27.520 --> 07:28.510
Why not?

07:28.780 --> 07:33.010
Nephy has a lot of friends in this town.
 A fight will lead to casualties.

07:37.130 --> 07:41.010
Come along, Lady Chastille! 
Cardinal Clavwell is calling for you.

07:41.010 --> 07:42.570
Cardinal Clavwell?

07:42.570 --> 07:44.940
Please, worry more about your self!

07:44.940 --> 07:47.080
Hey, wait...

07:45.840 --> 07:47.080
Come, right this way!

07:47.080 --> 07:49.200
Fine, just stop pushing me!

07:47.080 --> 07:49.950
Do you think Miss Chastille will be all right?

07:49.950 --> 07:51.260
Hard to say.

07:51.710 --> 07:56.490
But she's got plenty of support and
 other people she can count on.

07:57.040 --> 08:01.580
<i>Being a sorcerer, if I got involved, 
it'd make her position more precarious.</i>

08:02.130 --> 08:05.790
I'm curious, For. 
Did they do something to you?

08:06.210 --> 08:09.460
Does a sorcerer really need a 
reason to hate the Angelic Knights?

08:10.380 --> 08:13.340
No. It's perfectly natural.

08:15.680 --> 08:18.200
<i>Here's hoping this doesn't 
lead to more trouble.</i>

08:26.490 --> 08:28.160
This is the Archdemon's castle.

08:28.660 --> 08:30.970
I can't believe there's a building 
like this underground.

08:31.990 --> 08:34.610
It was probably constructed on the surface.

08:34.610 --> 08:37.320
Marchosias most likely used 
sorcery to lower it down.

08:40.110 --> 08:43.080
Something about it smells familiar.

08:43.370 --> 08:44.400
What?

08:44.400 --> 08:45.290
I think...

08:47.040 --> 08:49.290
that dragons used to live here.

08:49.550 --> 08:50.850
Are you certain?

08:50.850 --> 08:54.010
The way the cave is shaped reminds 
me of the one I used to live in.

08:54.440 --> 08:55.880
The smell of the mana, too.

08:56.290 --> 09:00.350
Okay, see if you can find anything 
connected to dragons inside the castle.

09:00.620 --> 09:02.620
You can take any books you want.

09:02.620 --> 09:03.260
Okay.

09:31.240 --> 09:32.960
Zagan, what is that?

09:33.360 --> 09:35.430
Some kind of golem or chimera.

09:35.430 --> 09:37.880
A creature created with sorcery, in any case.

09:38.340 --> 09:40.580
Was it meant to guard this place?

09:40.580 --> 09:41.990
Most likely.

09:41.990 --> 09:46.230
But with Marchosias dead, 
it's stopped functioning.

09:46.740 --> 09:50.130
We'd better not risk it activating 
by touching it. Come on.

09:50.130 --> 09:51.230
R-Right.

09:57.040 --> 09:59.810
Zagan, what about that casting circle?

09:59.810 --> 10:01.030
What do you mean?

10:01.720 --> 10:03.740
It's got draconic patterns.

10:04.300 --> 10:05.350
Really?!

10:05.350 --> 10:06.120
Yeah.

10:06.490 --> 10:08.060
I found it for you.

10:08.510 --> 10:10.430
Right. Good work, For.

10:12.960 --> 10:14.660
Zagan praised me!

10:15.190 --> 10:17.220
That's great, For.

10:19.310 --> 10:21.410
Can you tell what it's function is?

10:21.410 --> 10:24.690
I think it's hiding a door or something.

10:24.690 --> 10:25.680
Can you open it?

10:26.160 --> 10:26.790
Yeah.

10:34.780 --> 10:35.900
What is it?

10:35.900 --> 10:37.700
Well, I just...

10:41.570 --> 10:42.780
<i>This is...</i>

10:43.150 --> 10:45.180
<i>She wants something?</i>

10:45.710 --> 10:46.660
<i>But what?</i>

10:48.720 --> 10:50.750
<i>Oh, I see!</i>

10:51.910 --> 10:52.930
Nephy.

10:54.320 --> 10:57.260
Don't... move.

10:57.260 --> 10:58.720
R-Right!

11:01.220 --> 11:03.970
<b>Rub</b>

11:01.220 --> 11:03.970
<b>Rub</b>

11:01.220 --> 11:03.970
<b>Rub</b>

11:01.220 --> 11:03.970
<b>Rub</b>

11:06.970 --> 11:14.230
<b>Rub</b>

11:06.970 --> 11:14.230
<b>Rub</b>

11:07.600 --> 11:11.600
<i>She must've gotten jealous when 
she saw me pat For on the head.</i>

11:11.600 --> 11:14.230
<i>She never acted like that when 
it was just the two of us.</i>

11:14.900 --> 11:18.240
<i>This isn't bad at all.</i>

11:18.480 --> 11:20.030
Stare....

11:19.360 --> 11:20.030
Gasp

11:20.350 --> 11:22.270
Wh-What is it, For?!

11:22.270 --> 11:23.370
It's open.

11:23.760 --> 11:25.890
R-Right, good work!

11:44.890 --> 11:46.260
I see.

11:46.850 --> 11:49.230
Looks like this is the real deal.

11:53.380 --> 11:59.270
Our goal is to gather any books that have
 accounts of demons or the Archdemon crests.

11:59.270 --> 12:00.740
Understood.

12:04.930 --> 12:05.950
What is it?

12:05.950 --> 12:09.280
Zagan, can you read people's minds?

12:10.180 --> 12:12.160
Good question. I wonder...

12:12.500 --> 12:17.170
You were able to tell what Nephy 
wanted earlier without asking.

12:17.450 --> 12:22.150
Oh... Nephy always gives me clues.

12:22.150 --> 12:25.430
I need to be able to pick up
 on them, for my sake.

12:26.660 --> 12:29.180
I'm kinda jealous.

12:29.180 --> 12:31.350
Not sure why you're acting like an outsider.

12:32.490 --> 12:37.480
I don't know how long dragons live, but 
Marchosias was around for a thousand years.

12:37.870 --> 12:43.610
I'm sure you'll be able to tell what people 
want without asking if you live that long, too.

12:44.050 --> 12:45.130
A thousand years...

12:45.760 --> 12:47.370
And I can stay with you?

12:47.710 --> 12:51.330
I won't stop you if you try to leave.

12:53.450 --> 12:54.920
I'm staying here!

12:56.200 --> 12:58.750
<i>This really isn't like me...</i>

13:03.970 --> 13:05.630
"The 12 Sacred Swords."

13:06.950 --> 13:07.950
Let me see that!

13:12.160 --> 13:13.140
I knew it!

13:13.810 --> 13:19.400
When I saw the Archdemon crest, I thought 
I had seen something similar before...

13:19.400 --> 13:21.980
It's the writing that's engraved 
on the Sacred Swords!

13:21.980 --> 13:26.820
It's not exactly the same, but I can tell 
they're scripts that come from the same source.

13:27.310 --> 13:28.870
You've done it, For!

13:29.410 --> 13:30.460
This means...

13:30.910 --> 13:36.040
If I learn more about Sacred Swords, 
I can find out about the Archdemon crests!

13:36.040 --> 13:41.040
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

13:50.570 --> 13:52.390
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance...

13:53.120 --> 13:56.850
Lord of the Angelic Knights, 
Sir Raphael Hyurandell.

13:57.140 --> 14:01.610
And you must be the Maiden of the 
Sacred Sword I've heard so much about.

14:02.100 --> 14:05.100
I was informed you'd been relieved 
of duty for defying orders,

14:05.100 --> 14:07.490
but you've got a good look to you.

14:08.540 --> 14:10.660
Your praise honors me.

14:10.940 --> 14:11.780
So...

14:12.240 --> 14:15.520
How many sorcerers have you slain?

14:16.990 --> 14:18.500
<i>Straight to the point, huh?</i>

14:19.260 --> 14:23.120
<i>The wielder of a Sacred Sword who has 
slain the greatest number of sorcerers...</i>

14:23.120 --> 14:27.300
<i>He'd gladly take my head 
after my act of apostasy.</i>

14:27.800 --> 14:29.180
<i>So be it, then!</i>

14:29.970 --> 14:33.220
I do not believe that to 
be a number to boast about.

14:35.120 --> 14:38.480
Lady Chastille! Please, speak more carefully!

14:38.480 --> 14:41.400
I'm not sure how much we can protect you!

14:41.400 --> 14:42.860
This is pitiful!

14:42.860 --> 14:46.190
Haven't we all pledged to give our 
lives to protect Lady Chastille?!

14:49.170 --> 14:53.200
It's been a long time since I've met anyone 
who'd dare talk to me like that.

14:53.630 --> 14:56.620
And you might be the first woman to do it.

14:57.150 --> 15:00.120
You can take that honor 
with you to the afterlife.

15:02.170 --> 15:03.900
Please run, Lady Chastille!

15:03.900 --> 15:05.240
Sir Raphael!

15:06.230 --> 15:08.880
What do you think you're doing to my knights?

15:09.650 --> 15:15.720
Clavwell, eh? I have no business
 with a bureaucrat like you.

15:16.020 --> 15:20.690
Be that as it may, I have a 
duty to protect these knights.

15:22.040 --> 15:26.920
Never mind that. You confiscated the 
woman's Sacred Sword, didn't you?

15:26.920 --> 15:28.400
Where is it?

15:28.720 --> 15:31.600
What does it matter to you?

15:31.600 --> 15:33.200
That should be obvious.

15:33.740 --> 15:36.910
Sacred Swords choose their wielders.

15:36.910 --> 15:41.680
As long as that chosen person lives, 
the sword cannot be used by anyone else.

15:41.680 --> 15:43.040
So...

15:43.330 --> 15:46.600
perhaps I should relieve the girl of her head.

15:47.170 --> 15:49.380
Of all the dreadful ideas!

15:49.720 --> 15:51.540
I was merely stating a fact.

15:51.540 --> 15:57.470
Besides, you're in no position to dictate what a 
Sacred Sword wielder does with their blade.

15:57.790 --> 16:00.550
You speak out of turn, Sir Raphael!

16:00.550 --> 16:06.940
If we wield our swords on our own whims, 
then we're no better than thugs!

16:08.730 --> 16:12.570
That makes a second time 
you've taken that tone with me!

16:12.570 --> 16:14.030
Interesting!

16:15.830 --> 16:17.370
Is this what you want, Clavwell?

16:17.640 --> 16:23.670
One of the knights you aim to protect is on 
the verge of being slain while unarmed.

16:26.960 --> 16:28.680
V-Very well.

16:29.400 --> 16:31.580
Chastille, come this way.

16:38.720 --> 16:39.680
Take it.

16:40.230 --> 16:45.240
I don't know if returning this 
to you is the right choice.

16:45.240 --> 16:50.690
I may even be giving that man 
an excuse to cut you down.

16:50.690 --> 16:57.360
But... I have faith that you will find 
a way to overcome this tribulation.

17:00.480 --> 17:01.910
Thank you, Your Excellency.

17:04.190 --> 17:05.420
<i>That man...</i>

17:06.340 --> 17:09.670
<i>It's like he was manipulating 
the sword back into my hands.</i>

17:10.280 --> 17:11.690
<i>But why?</i>

17:24.390 --> 17:28.190
Y-You're actually living 
with a little girl now?!

17:29.180 --> 17:31.950
How do you even know about that, Barbatos?

17:31.950 --> 17:34.440
And I thought your only joke was your face!

17:34.820 --> 17:38.770
There have been rumors around town 
about you kidnapping some brat!

17:38.770 --> 17:42.100
Are we done now? Can I go?

17:42.100 --> 17:45.810
Damn, man, don't be such a stiff!

17:45.810 --> 17:48.710
I'm treating you to 
good booze here, y'know?

17:50.120 --> 17:53.460
So, who exactly is this rumored kid?

17:53.460 --> 17:56.610
You take in a second apprentice or something?

17:56.610 --> 17:58.010
<i>He's half right.</i>

17:58.510 --> 18:01.050
It's actually someone you know.

18:01.340 --> 18:02.160
What?!

18:02.160 --> 18:03.890
So she's a sorcerer?

18:05.170 --> 18:07.730
A female sorcerer...

18:07.730 --> 18:10.300
I think the only local is 
Gremory the Enchantress?

18:10.300 --> 18:13.150
She's supposed to be a 
serious man-hater, though...

18:13.570 --> 18:19.030
<i>It doesn't look like he realizes 
For is Valefor... or a dragon—</i>

18:19.030 --> 18:20.620
Oh, yeah, Valefor!

18:22.220 --> 18:25.880
Didn't Valefor raid your place the other day?

18:25.880 --> 18:27.820
The giant guy in the mask.

18:27.820 --> 18:30.720
Right... that did happen.

18:30.720 --> 18:32.250
Whatever happened with him?

18:32.580 --> 18:34.800
Survived, with any luck.

18:35.120 --> 18:38.170
What, you just tossed him out like usual?

18:38.980 --> 18:42.550
There are rumors that he's a dragon, y'know.

18:42.550 --> 18:46.240
You could make some real potent 
catalysts out of his corpse.

18:46.240 --> 18:47.520
What a waste.

18:47.850 --> 18:52.110
<i>A good example of why I should 
keep For's identity a secret...</i>

18:52.520 --> 18:55.650
Well, forget about Valefor.
 Let's talk about this kid you've grabbed.

18:55.650 --> 18:56.790
Who is she?

18:56.790 --> 19:00.160
<i>Okay, does he actually know or not?</i>

19:00.870 --> 19:03.990
It's hard to explain. I guess 
we could say I've adopted her.

19:05.220 --> 19:08.100
Y-You, adopted a little girl?!

19:08.750 --> 19:10.250
<i>Oh, he's so far gone.</i>

19:11.050 --> 19:14.290
Well, that's enough joking for now.

19:14.640 --> 19:16.250
Can we finally get to the point, then?

19:17.560 --> 19:22.640
The Church has sent for a real troublemaker. 
Thought I'd let you know.

19:23.170 --> 19:25.700
The sorcerer hunter, Raphael.

19:25.700 --> 19:29.260
He's killed 499 sorcerers so far!

19:29.730 --> 19:33.980
The most dreadful of the Sacred Sword users, 
who's taken down the highest number of targets.

19:34.580 --> 19:38.570
And you've been chosen 
to be lucky number 500!

19:38.840 --> 19:40.240
That's odd.

19:40.240 --> 19:44.160
Even with a Sacred Sword, could one 
person kill that many sorcerers?

19:44.160 --> 19:45.580
That's the thing...

19:45.950 --> 19:48.910
They say he's eaten a dragon.

19:50.450 --> 19:54.630
Humans think that eating 
dragon flesh will make them stronger.

19:54.880 --> 19:58.250
Does a sorcerer really need a 
reason to hate the Angelic Knights?

19:58.970 --> 20:00.760
<i>That explains it.</i>

20:01.100 --> 20:06.300
The Church doesn't approve of eating dragons, 
so this all all unconfirmed, mind you.

20:06.720 --> 20:10.100
You're volunteering an 
awful lot of news today.

20:11.120 --> 20:15.530
Well, let's chalk it up to trying 
to make up for the other day.

20:16.630 --> 20:21.750
I figure cozying up with you is gonna be a 
sweeter deal for me than trying to kill you!

20:21.750 --> 20:23.910
You're as shameless as you are obnoxious.

20:24.400 --> 20:25.910
What I am is handy!

20:26.340 --> 20:29.340
This would be a good deal for you.

20:29.340 --> 20:33.250
Maybe I'd believe that if 
I thought you had a conscience.

20:33.600 --> 20:34.960
What do you really want?

20:35.410 --> 20:37.600
Marchosias' estate...

20:37.600 --> 20:40.400
Why don't you let me manage it for you?

20:40.400 --> 20:42.630
It's not like you can handle it all on your—

20:41.800 --> 20:43.260
No, thank you.

20:43.260 --> 20:44.550
Why, dammit?!

20:44.550 --> 20:48.810
Because you're gonna hide anything 
you don't want me seeing.

20:49.150 --> 20:51.560
Well, obviously! 
What's the problem with that?

20:52.090 --> 20:55.690
<i>I... cannot understand how someone 
as smart as him can be so stupid.</i>

20:56.360 --> 20:58.860
You can have a few sorcerous tomes.

20:58.860 --> 21:00.230
That'll have to do.

21:01.900 --> 21:04.150
I guess that's a fair deal.

21:04.450 --> 21:07.410
Gotta admit, it's great 
having generous friends!

21:08.000 --> 21:12.580
I get to pick the books 
I want though, got it?

21:12.580 --> 21:14.700
Don't try and pawn any crap off on me—

21:14.700 --> 21:16.310
One thing, Barbatos.

21:17.300 --> 21:21.500
The dragon-slaying Angelic Knight 
you mentioned, what's he look like?

21:21.830 --> 21:28.080
Let's see... he's supposed to be 
way too huge for how old he is.

21:28.080 --> 21:32.430
He's got a big scar from his forehead 
across the left side of his face.

21:33.250 --> 21:36.300
They say the dragon he 
took down gave it to him.

21:37.360 --> 21:39.150
What a coincidence.

21:39.450 --> 21:42.230
I've seen someone who looks just like that.

21:42.230 --> 21:45.640
Well damn, I'm impressed you survived!

21:45.640 --> 21:48.320
I figured he would've taken 
a swing at you on sight.

21:50.260 --> 21:53.830
I think... we're just getting to that part.

23:30.050 --> 23:35.050
<b>Next Time: 
The Angelic Knight Situation Sounds Like
 a Mess I'd Rather Not Get Involved In</b>
